; =====================================================================
; ijson-types.cddl
;
; VERBATIM.  RFC 8610's own bytes, copied unchanged.  NOT authored by
; this project.  Do not edit, correct or reformat it.
;
; Locator:  RFC 8610, Appendix E (Figure 16: I-JSON Types for CDDL (Not
;           Part of Prelude)).  Source text lines 3050-3052.
;           <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610.txt>
;
; Source digest (sha256 of the full cached source text):
;   3713f2a50e23a2bea0a6147ad6c4433605a00c3d00a868bfa86a42b204997089
;
; NOT PART OF THE PRELUDE.  The RFC is explicit, quoted (source lines
; 3046-3048): "Note that the types given here are not part of the
; prelude; they need to be copied into the CDDL specification if
; needed."  They exist because I-JSON [RFC7493] parses numbers into
; float64, so only integers in [-(2**53)+1, (2**53)-1] survive
; interchange -- a narrower range than CDDL "int".
; =====================================================================

; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM E-16 (source lines 3050-3052, sha256 258562bcda534cd9cb20a8fcf838e9f01feceabc7db57ea2d54dbf29636c331e) ----
               ij-uint = 0..9007199254740991
               ij-nint = -9007199254740991..-1
               ij-int = -9007199254740991..9007199254740991
; ---- END VERBATIM E-16 ----
